I registered NDMAKE 4.31 and received several executables, including MAKE43L.EXE
which handles larger problems without running out of memory. The distribution
explicitly stated that this version was not shareware. As far as I know Mr.
Kneller gave up on shareware distribution shortly after this release and
any recent versions are commercial products.  A major shame since this is
an excellent product made even better by its very low price compared with
what MKS, Polytron, and others want.

Often if you run make again, it can complete without running out of memory.
Otherwise you need to split it up into two or more separate make files.

